From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0922 redfin: camera capture path, step 2: a sensor's own frames

"c 21 SENSOR MODE OPTIONS" (sweetcam=2): HackiOS redwood_camera.c cam=4 with
redfin's sensors. camcc PLL2 (Zonda, 960 MHz, cam_cc_pll2_config) for the
24 MHz MCLK (aux /2, M/N 1/20) the device tree and the sensors' tables ask
for; the sensor powered up as for "c N", its chip ID, its "init" and "resM"
tables from /private/var/local/fw/camera-<sensor>.tab (tools/redfin-camtab.py,
out of the vendor's module file: on the phone only); CSID-lite 0 from the
sensor's CSIPHY into RDI 0 and IFE-lite 0's write master; the CSIPHY
(v1.2.2: the 1.2 tables, D-PHY, four lanes) with refgen on; "on", the
frames, the write master stopped at the wanted one, "off"; all undone.

"c 20" and "c 21" run on a thread of their own: a poke runs on the USB
driver's command thread, which also sends the log, so r17a/r17b's c 20 went
down with none of its lines out. The CCI pins are held as I2C lines for a
whole session of writes and given back clock line first. "c 22 MS" sets
the time before each stage (the UDP log drops what a poke's run prints;
the ring, read with klog, has it). The SMMU is mapped whole: 0921 mapped
128 KB and then read the context banks' SCTLRs at 512 KB and up.

